/* book exam traps: Precession is at right angles to the push: carry the push 90° round in the direction of spin. Drawing the axis moving along the push loses the marks. | Convert rpm to rad/s before Ω = T/(Iω). Using rpm directly makes Ω come out 9.55 times too small (the wrong answer is the right one × 2π/60). | Nutation is a short transient after a sudden torque; precession is the steady motion. Do not swap them. | Apparent drift is the Earth turning under a fixed axis; real drift is from friction and imbalance. Only real drift is cured by a better gyro. | A turn coordinator shows rate of turn, not bank angle; it is an SDF rate gyro, not a vertical gyro. */
